 "fim_caveat": "The FRF-FIM is a LINEARIZATION at nominal theta. The whole log|H| likelihood is hyper-sensitive near resonances (d log|H|/d theta blows up at resonance edges), so the FIM over 960 freq x sensor points is INFLATED and reports many theta combinations above prior precision -- optimistic. The robust aggregate signal measure is the strain-energy table (only 4/9 groups store >5% mean modal SE); the OPERATIVE identifiability test is the nonlinear posterior RECOVERY in the sweep cells (covered/informed flags), which accounts for theta<->discrepancy confounding the linear FIM misses.",
 "note": "identifiability tied to the realized discrepancy floor (sigma_d~0.08); a group with ample strain energy can still fail to separate if its FRF signal sits below that floor. The Schneider discrepancy is SMOOTH, so it does not mask the SHARP resonance-shift theta signal -- which is why identifiable groups can still be recovered with the discrepancy present."
}